Z||000002||Bob Englert||03-12-2001||08:24 PM||||It worked for me on my 87 GT.  <P>I noticed in the instructions that the wire you cut COULD be on another pin besides the one in the diagram.  It says to verify the wire color to be sure.  <P>Could this be the problem with your mod?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000003||pherder||03-12-2001||08:31 PM||||One other thing to check.<P>When I did the "fix", it didn't work either <B>BUT</B> when I checked out my wiring, I found that the instrutment cluster plastic wiring ends that the electric plugs plug into had shifted and I was shorting out other lines on the cluster and <B>that</B> was putting 12 VDC to the water temp gauge!<P>Got the little "legs" of the plastic to lay down straight and haven't had a problem since.<P>Paul<P>------------------<BR>88 Formula<BR>88 Coupe<BR>86 SE<BR>95 GMC<BR>92 Mazda<BR>55 Jones<BR>Sedgwick, KS 67135<BR>pherder@kscable.com||||reg||1
