Z||000005||KissMySSFiero||03-13-2001||10:10 PM||||what are the symptoms to this?<BR>on my car the temp gauge gets pegged alot of the time but a light tap on the guage pod and it pops back to norm.  i thought it was because i bent something when i had my guage cluster apart.  is this the samething that happens to other cars?<BR>TIA<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:KissMySSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:KissMySSFiero@netzero.net">KissMySSFiero@netzero.net</A>    <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">        <BR>"There's a fine line between love and beer"||||reg||1
Z||000006||Bob Englert||03-13-2001||10:32 PM||||KissMySSFiero<P>You described the problem exactly.  The gauge gets full 12V during cranking, causing the needle to swing violently to full scale.<P>On my blue GT, the needle almost always sticks and requires a hard rap on the top of the instrument cluster to free.  Not very elegant and can't be good for the gauges.  On my maroon GT the needle hit so hard that it actually rotated on the shaft of the gauge.  This caused the gauge to read at the first mark (100°) instead of the second major mark at normal temp.  I had to disassemble the temp gauge and pull the needle off and replace it in the right position.  On some cars the problem can actually cause the needle to fall off the shaft.<P>The fix worked well for me on the maroon GT.  I took the time to polish the clear gauge cover while it was apart during the repair.  I just need to get it done to the blue GT so I can stop banging on the instrument cluster!<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
